# Rust — the bootstrap compiler is archived (M-bootstrap-archive), and so is
# everything cargo writes. The old `/target` stays listed for one reason: a
# checkout made before the archive still has one.
/target
archive/bootstrap-rs/target

# heroes build cache (generated C, runtime.o, binaries — all derived)
/build

# The compiler itself. Both names are in CLAUDE.md § Commands: `heroes` is what
# the one clang line over `seed/heroes.c` produces, and `heroes-next` is what
# that binary builds from `selfhost/main.hero`. Every checkout that follows the
# README makes one, and a parallel session staging with `git add -A` would
# commit a multi-megabyte binary that nothing in this repository reads.
/heroes
/heroes-next

# The third name, and it was missing until 2026-09-05 while the other two had a
# paragraph explaining why they are here. `heroes-from-seed` is what CI builds
# from `seed/heroes.c` on every leg, it is the FIRST candidate
# `tests/harness/shell.hero`'s `some_compiler()` looks for, and it is the binary
# a session reaches for when it wants to know what a clean checkout would do. It
# is the same multi-megabyte artifact as the two above, and it was one `git add
# -A` away from the repository the whole time.
/heroes-from-seed

# bootstrap stages (derived)
stage[0-9]
*.o

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Scratch git worktrees created by panel judges (never project content).
.claude/worktrees/

# Python's bytecode cache. The only Python here is `.claude/hooks/`, and it
# leaves no cache when the harness runs it as a script; a cache appears the
# moment somebody IMPORTS a hook to test it, which is how the guard's
# seventeen shapes were checked on 2026-09-08. Nothing here should ever be
# committed and nothing reads it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# One assistant's local permission allow-list, which is per-machine and names
# paths outside this repository. It was kept out by the author's GLOBAL ignore
# file and by nothing here, so a fresh clone and a CI checkout had no rule for
# it at all; the protection moves into the repository on 2026-09-08, where the
# tree that needs it can carry it (M-open-repository). `.claude/settings.json`
# is the shared one and stays tracked.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Secrets. The Cloudflare API token that deploys the site lives in `.env` at the
# repository root, and nothing that runs here reads it: the deploy reads it from
# GitHub's secret store instead. `.env.example` is the documented shape, carries
# no value, and is the one name this pattern lets back in. The `.env.*` line is
# not redundant — it is what catches `.env.local` and `.env.production`, which
# are the names a tool invents when nobody was looking.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Wrangler's local state: a cached `request.cf` object and miniflare's cache.
# Derived, per-machine, and written by a `wrangler` invocation rather than by
# anybody. Never project content.
.wrangler/
